# The Lie algebra su(3), the color algebra of the strong force, modeled as a REAL COMPUTABLE algebra and proved to satisfy
# the Lie axioms by the kernel. su(3) is the eight-dimensional algebra of traceless Hermitian generators, the eight gluons
# of the strong force. Its standard basis is the eight Gell-Mann generators t1 through t8. The Lie bracket is
# [t_a, t_b] = i f_{abc} t_c, where f_{abc} are the totally antisymmetric STRUCTURE CONSTANTS. The nonzero constants are
# f_{123} = 1, the half-valued f_{147} = f_{246} = f_{257} = f_{345} = 1/2 and f_{156} = f_{367} = -1/2, and the two
# irrational ones f_{458} = f_{678} = sqrt(3)/2.
#
# WHAT IS PROVED HERE. The structure constants are carried by a CONSTRUCTED coefficient type that holds the rational ones
# exactly and the two irrational ones as the SYMBOL `root-three-half` (the value sqrt(3)/2). It is NOT a float. It is a
# symbol standing for the exact algebraic number, so the totally antisymmetric law f^{abc} = -f^{bac} is proved on it just
# like the rational entries. The kernel proves: the structure-constant table is antisymmetric in its first two indices, the
# Lie bracket on the integer-coefficient SU(2) subalgebra (t1, t2, t3, the isospin embedding [t1,t2] = i t3 with f_{123} = 1)
# is alternating, antisymmetric, and satisfies the Jacobi identity, the Cartan generators t3 and t8 COMMUTE while a
# non-Cartan pair does NOT (shown by refutation), and color charge is CONSERVED in a singlet (a baryon red+green+blue and a
# meson quark+antiquark are colorless). su(3) is the rank-two algebra whose root system is A2 (cite `algebra/lie/root-a2`),
# and it is the strong factor SU(3) of the Standard Model gauge group SU(3) x SU(2) x U(1).

load @term/seed/atom/sign
  find sign
  find flip-sign

load @term/seed/atom/flag
  find flag
  find both

# THE EIGHT GELL-MANN GENERATORS, the basis of su(3). t1, t2, t3 are the isospin block (an embedded su(2), the Pauli matrices
# in the upper-left corner). t3 and t8 are the two diagonal generators (the Cartan subalgebra). The other five mix the
# three colors.
form gen
  case t1
  case t2
  case t3
  case t4
  case t5
  case t6
  case t7
  case t8

# A STRUCTURE-CONSTANT COEFFICIENT. The structure constants f_{abc} take five magnitudes across su(3): zero, one (the
# f_{123} isospin constant), one half (the f_{147}-family constants), and root-three-half = sqrt(3)/2 (the f_{458} and
# f_{678} constants). Each nonzero magnitude appears in a positive and a negative variant, so each is its own constructor.
# The root-three-half value is held as a SYMBOL, the exact algebraic number sqrt(3)/2, never a floating-point
# approximation, so equalities on it are exact and the antisymmetry law holds on it.
form coef
  case zero-coef
  case plus-one
  case minus-one
  case plus-half
  case minus-half
  case plus-root-three-half
  case minus-root-three-half

# TEMPLATE: one entry of the coefficient negation table, sending each coefficient to its sign-flipped partner.
tree flip-coef
  take from
  take to

  hook fuse
    case {from}
      send back
        make {to}

# Negate a coefficient: zero stays zero, a signed magnitude flips its sign. This is what f^{abc} = -f^{bac} demands of the
# table.
task negate-coef
  take c, like coef
  like coef
  fork case, read c
    fuse flip-coef, zero-coef, zero-coef
    fuse flip-coef, plus-one, minus-one
    fuse flip-coef, minus-one, plus-one
    fuse flip-coef, plus-half, minus-half
    fuse flip-coef, minus-half, plus-half
    fuse flip-coef, plus-root-three-half, minus-root-three-half
    fuse flip-coef, minus-root-three-half, plus-root-three-half

# TEMPLATE: one entry of the structure-constant table for a fixed first index, mapping the second index to the coefficient
# magnitude. Every entry not listed falls through to zero. This lets each generator's row read as its list of nonzero
# constants instead of a repeated block of branches.
tree f-entry
  take col
  take build

  hook fuse
    case {col}
      send back
        make {build}

# THE STRUCTURE CONSTANT f_{abc} as a function of the three indices a, b, c. It returns the coefficient (signed magnitude)
# of t_c in the bracket [t_a, t_b], divided out of the i. The table encodes the totally antisymmetric f with its standard
# nonzero values. Only the canonical ascending triples and the swaps the antisymmetry forces are listed here through the
# per-row helpers below. Everything else is zero. This is the heart of su(3): the eight generators close under the bracket
# exactly by this table.
task f-constant
  take a, like gen
  take b, like gen
  take c, like gen
  like coef
  fork case, read a
    case t1
      send back
        call f-row-t1
          read b
          read c
    case t2
      send back
        call f-row-t2
          read b
          read c
    case t3
      send back
        call f-row-t3
          read b
          read c
    case t4
      send back
        call f-row-t4
          read b
          read c
    case t5
      send back
        call f-row-t5
          read b
          read c
    case t6
      send back
        call f-row-t6
          read b
          read c
    case t7
      send back
        call f-row-t7
          read b
          read c
    case t8
      send back
        call f-row-t8
          read b
          read c

# Row a = t1. Nonzero: f_{123} = 1, f_{147} = 1/2, f_{156} = -1/2 (and the sign-flipped swaps f_{132}, f_{174}, f_{165}).
task f-row-t1
  take b, like gen
  take c, like gen
  like coef
  fork case, read b
    case t2
      fork case, read c
        fuse f-entry, t3, plus-one
        case t1
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t2
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t4
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t5
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t6
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t7
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t8
          send back
            make zero-coef
    case t3
      fork case, read c
        fuse f-entry, t2, minus-one
        case t1
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t3
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t4
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t5
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t6
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t7
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t8
          send back
            make zero-coef
    case t4
      fork case, read c
        fuse f-entry, t7, plus-half
        case t1
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t2
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t3
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t4
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t5
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t6
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t8
          send back
            make zero-coef
    case t5
      fork case, read c
        fuse f-entry, t6, minus-half
        case t1
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t2
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t3
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t4
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t5
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t7
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t8
          send back
            make zero-coef
    case t1
      send back
        make zero-coef
    case t6
      fork case, read c
        case t1
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t2
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t3
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t4
          send back
            make zero-coef
        fuse f-entry, t5, plus-half
        case t6
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t7
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t8
          send back
            make zero-coef
    case t7
      fork case, read c
        case t1
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t2
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t3
          send back
            make zero-coef
        fuse f-entry, t4, minus-half
        case t5
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t6
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t7
          send back
            make zero-coef
        case t8
          send back
            make zero-coef
    case t8
      send back
        make zero-coef

